nodo dataset.\nThe occurrences file includes a column called “summarized by” or something, containing the measurement ID of the summary record in the M\u0026F file.\nThe information from the occurrences file does not go into the graph, but the record with the summarized version will have a property, populated from a column in the M\u0026F file, called “additional metadata” or something, with a term definition explaining the relationship, and a value of [URL pointing to the occurrences file].\nList of tasks for Eli’s validation script\nWhen a trait data file is ready for publication, we should run a validation script on it to make sure there aren’t any loose ends:\nIf there is a Taxon file, update the eolID values in the Trait file to match the ones in the Taxon file.\nTrait file validation:\neolID values should match taxonID values in the reference hierarchy -\u003e report values that don’t have a match.\nstop nodes should descend from start nodes -\u003e report start/stop node pairs that are in violation. \nuris in the trait, value, lifestage, sex, …. columns should match uris in the terms file -\u003e report uris that don’t have a match\nreferenceIDs should have an identifier match in the References master file -\u003e automatically add missing identifiers, try to fetch bibliographic citation via CrossRef, WikiData, or another service, add identifiers that cannot be resolved to a manual reference curation doc.\n"},{"ty":"is","ibi":22542,"s":"\u0003\n"},{"ty":"ae","et":"list","id":"kix.4b8attvvjkz1","epm":{"le_nb":{"nl_4":{"b_gf":"%4.","b_ts":{"ts_un":false,"ts_un_i":false,"ts_sc":false,"ts_it_i":true,"ts_fgc2":{"hclr_color":"#000000","clr_type":0},"ts_st_i":true,"ts_bgc2":{"hclr_color":null,"clr_type":0},"ts_fs_i":true,"ts_ff_i":true,"ts_bgc2_i":true,"ts_it":false,"ts_va":"nor","ts_bd_i":true,"ts_va_i":true,"ts_fs":11.0,"ts_ff":"Arial","ts_st":false,"ts_bd":false,"ts_fgc2_i":true,"ts_sc_i":true,"ts_tw":400},"b_ifl":162.0,"b_gs":"","b_a":0,"b_sn":1,"b_gt":13,"b_il"